## Testing Strategy

- Write tests before fixing bugs
- Follow Arrange-Act-Assert pattern
- Maintain 80%+ code coverage minimum
- Test edge cases thoroughly
- Keep tests independent and isolated
- Use descriptive test names
- Group related tests with clarity

## Unit Testing Principles

- Test business logic in isolation
- Mock external dependencies completely
- Test error scenarios comprehensively
- Verify state transitions explicitly
- Test validators @lib/core/utils/validators.dart
- Test data transformations accurately
- Use test helpers @test/helpers/test_helpers.dart

```dart
// Example from project structure
test('should validate email correctly', () {
  // Arrange
  const email = 'test@example.com';

  // Act
  final result = validateEmail(email);

  // Assert
  expect(result, isTrue);
});

// Clean Architecture layer testing
test('should execute use case successfully', () {
  // Arrange
  final mockRepository = MockContactRepository();
  final useCase = GetContactsUseCase(mockRepository);
  when(() => mockRepository.findAll()).thenAnswer(
    (_) async => Right(mockContactList),
  );

  // Act
  final result = await useCase.execute();

  // Assert
  expect(result.isRight(), isTrue);
  verify(() => mockRepository.findAll()).called(1);
});
```

## Widget Testing Standards

- Test UI components in isolation
- Verify widget interactions accurately
- Test widget state changes
- Mock dependencies with test doubles
- Use `pumpWidget` for rendering setup
- Apply `pump` for animation testing
- Test golden files for regression

```dart
testWidgets('should display loading state correctly', (tester) async {
  // Arrange
  await TestHelpers.setupMockFallbacks();

  // Act
  await tester.pumpWidget(MaterialApp(
    home: LoadingWidget(),
  ));

  // Assert
  expect(find.byType(CircularProgressIndicator), findsOneWidget);
});
```

## Clean Architecture Testing

- Test domain entities independently
- Mock repository interfaces @lib/db/interfaces/
- Test use cases without dependencies
- Verify data layer mappings
- Test presentation layer controllers
- Mock service interfaces @lib/services/interfaces/
- Test adapter implementations separately

## Mock Management

- Use established mocks @test/mocks/mock_services.dart
- Prefer fakes over complex mocks
- Use `mocktail` for interface mocking
- Register fallback values properly
- Mock at architectural boundaries only
- Keep mock behavior simple
- Document mock expectations clearly

```dart
// Using project's mock setup
class MockContactRepository extends Mock implements ContactRepository {}

void main() {
  setUpAll(() {
    TestHelpers.setupMockFallbacks();
  });
}
```

## Test Organization Rules

- Mirror lib/ structure in test/
- One test file per source
- Group by feature modules
- Use clear descriptive names
- Separate unit/widget/integration clearly
- Share utilities @test/helpers/test_helpers.dart
- Follow consistent naming conventions

## Test Data Management

- Use TestHelpers.createTestEntityMap() for entities
- Create mock DateTime consistently
- Use createMockDateTime() for timestamps
- Maintain test data factories
- Isolate test data creation
- Avoid hardcoded test values
- Use meaningful test scenarios

## Testing Commands Reference

- Run all tests: `flutter test`
- Generate coverage: `flutter test --coverage`
- Run specific file: `flutter test path/to/test.dart`
- Run integration tests: `flutter test integration_test`
- Watch mode development: `flutter test --watch`
- Verbose output: `flutter test --reporter=expanded`
- Profile test performance: `flutter test --profile`

## Coverage Requirements

- Minimum 80% line coverage required
- Include branch coverage validation
- Exclude generated files appropriately
- Monitor coverage trends continuously
- Report coverage @coverage/lcov.info
- Validate coverage in CI/CD
- Track coverage per feature

